   "text": {
    "L1": "Lines are parallel when they go in the same direction and never meet, even when extended.",
    "L2": "Their gap stays the same everywhere. Their lengths may be different.",
    "L3": "For AB and CD, the gap is 3 centimetres at the left, middle, and right.",
    "L4": "Because the gap stays the same, AB and CD are parallel.",
    "L5": "If the gap shrinks, the lines will meet when extended. Not meeting on this page is not enough.",
    "L6": "Perpendicular lines meet at a right angle. All four angles at the crossing are 90 degrees.",
    "L7": "The lines may be tilted; they do not need to stand upright. Now choose the reliable parallel-line test."
   },
